# text = The glare and hurry of broad noon are not adapted to idle pursuits like mine ; a glimpse of passing faces caught by the light of a street-lamp or a shop window is often better for my purpose than their full revelation in the daylight ; and , if I must add the truth , night is kinder in this respect than day , which too often destroys an air-built castle at the moment of its completion , without the least ceremony or remorse .
