# text = He was a young man of one-and-twenty or thereabouts ; well made , and certainly handsome , though the expression of his face was far from prepossessing , having in common with his manner and even his dress , a dissipated , insolent air which repelled one said the young fellow said the old man bitterly returned the other cried the old man , turning from him to me he added , in a lower voice as he drew closer to me said the young fellow catching at the word Saying this , he stepped to the door , and looking down the street beckoned several times to some unseen person , who , to judge from the air of impatience with which these signals were accompanied , required a great quantity of persuasion to induce him to advance .
