# text = The child advanced timidly towards her brother and put her hand in his , the dwarf ( if we may call him so ) glanced keenly at all present , and the curiosity-dealer , who plainly had not expected his uncouth visitor , seemed disconcerted and embarrassed said the dwarf , who with his hand stretched out above his eyes had been surveying the young man attentively replied the old man said the dwarf , pointing to Dick Swiveller said the old man inquired the dwarf , wheeling round and pointing straight at me The little man turned to the child as if to chide her or express his wonder , but as she was talking to the young man , held his peace , and bent his head to listen said the young fellow aloud cried the child pursued her brother with a sneer she returned he said , darting a bitter look at the grandfather said the child the child repeated with great emotion said the young man , as he stooped carelessly over the child , and having kissed her , pushed her from him He remained silent , following her with his eyes , until she had gained her little room and closed the door ; and then turning to the dwarf , said abruptly returned the dwarf pursued the other said Mr Quilp emphatically replied Quilp , with equal dryness cried Mr Swiveller , as his companion turned toward the door said Mr Quilp , to whom the monosyllable was addressed said Mr Swiveller said Daniel Quilp ; for the orator had made a sudden stop Without waiting for the permission he sought , Mr Swiveller stepped up to the dwarf , and leaning on his shoulder and stooping down to get at his ear , said in a voice which was perfectly audible to all present demanded Quilp replied Mr Swiveller slapping his picket
