# text = Nor did the striking of the clocks , hour after hour , appear to inspire him with any sense of drowsiness or any natural desire to go to rest , but rather to increase his wakefulness , which he showed , at every such indication of the progress of the night , by a suppressed cackling in his throat , and a motion of his shoulders , like one who laughs heartily but the same time slyly and by stealth .
