# text = The spot was at Chesea , for there Miss Sophia Wackles resided with her widowed mother and two sisters , in conjunction with whom she maintained a very small day-school for young ladies of proportionate dimensions ; a circumstance which was made known to the neighbourhood by an oval board over the front first-floor windows , whereupon appeared in circumbmbient flourishes the words ' Ladies' Seminary '; and which was further published and proclaimed at intervals between the hours of half-past nine and ten in the morning , by a straggling and solitrary young lady of tender years standing on the scraper on the tips of her toes and making futile attempts to reach the knocker with spelling-book .
# sent_id = 328
