# text = Late as the Dutch clock ' showed it to be , the poor woman was still hard at work at an ironing-table ; a young child lay sleeping in a cradle near the fire ; and another , a sturdy boy of two or three years old , very wide awake , with a very tight night-cap on his head , and a night-gown very much too small for him on his body , was sitting bolt upright in a clothes-basket , staring over the rim with his great round eyes , and looking as if he had thoroughly made up his mind never to go to sleep any more ; which , as he had already declined to take his natural rest and had been brought out of bed in consequence , opened a cheerful prospect for his relations and friends .
