# text = And now Mr Thomas Codlin , the misanthrope , after blowing away at the Pan's pipes until he was intensely wretched , took his station on one side of the checked drapery which concealed the mover of the figures , and putting his hands in his pockets prepared to reply to all questions and remarks of Punch , and to make a dismal feint of being his most intimate private friend , of believing in him to the fullest and most unlimited extent , of knowing that he enjoyed day and night a merry and glorious existence in that temple , and that he was at all times and under every circumstance the same intelligent and joyful person that the spectators then beheld him .
