# text = Frequently raising her eyes to the trees whence these sounds came down , and feeling as though they made the place more quiet than perfect silence would have done , the child loitered from grave to grave , now stopping to replace with careful hands the bramble which had started from some green mound it helped to keep in shape , and now peeping through one of the low latticed windows into the church , with its worm-eaten books upon the desks , and baize of whitened-green mouldering from the pew sides and leaving the naked wood to view .
