# text = And now that five-and-fifty years were gone , she spoke of the dead man as if he had been her son or grandson , with a kind of pity for his youth , growing out of her own old age , and an exalting of his strength and manly beauty as compared with her own weakness and decay ; and yet she spoke about him as her husband too , and thinking of herself in connexion with him , as she used to be and not as she was now , talked of their meeting in another world , as if he were dead but yesterday , and she , separated from her former self , were thinking of the happiness of that comely girl who seemed to have died with him .
