# text = As the travellers had observed that day many indications of their drawing nearer and nearer to the race town , such as gipsy camps , carts laden with gambling booths and their appurtenances , itinerant showmen of various kinds , and beggars and trampers of every degree , all wending their way in the same direction , Mr Codlin was fearful of finding the accommodations forestalled ; this fear increasing as he diminished the distance between himself and the hostelry , he quickened his pace , and notwithstanding the burden he had to carry , maintained a round trot until he reached the threshold .
