# text = Short shook his head , and wished he knew himself asked the host , turning to Mr Codlin he replied said Short growled Mr Codlin , glancing at the clock retorted his friend growled Mr Codlin , again glancing at the clock and from it to the cauldron returned Short muttered Thomas Codlin said Short cried Mr Codlin , glancing at the clock again and pulling his hair with both hands in a kind of frenzy , but whether occasioned by his companion's observation or the tardy pace of Time , it was difficult to determine repeated Short emphatically and slowly said Mr Codlin , who with his head upon his hands , and his elbows on his knees , had been shaking himself impatiently from side to side up to this point and occasionally stamping on the ground , but who now looked up with eager eyes His companion had only time to nod a brief assent to this position , for the child awoke at the instant .
