# text = Nor was this the only remarkable circumstance about these dogs , for each of them wore a kind of little coat of some gaudy colour trimmed with tarnished spangles , and one of them had a cap upon his head , tied very carefully under his chin , which had fallen down upon his nose and completely obscured one eye ; add to this , that the gaudy coats were all wet through and discoloured with rain , and that the wearers were splashed and dirty , and some idea may be formed of the unusual appearance of these new visitors to the Jolly Sandboys .
