# text = On every piece of waste or common ground , some small gambler drove his noisy trade , and bellowed to the idle passersby to stop and try their chance ; the crowd grew thicker and more noisy ; gilt gingerbread in blanket-stalls exposed its glories to the dust ; and often a four-horse carriage , dashing by , obscured all objects in the gritty cloud it raised , and left them , stunned and blinded , far behind .
