# text = The child bore upon her arm the little basket with her flowers , and sometimes stopped , with timid and modest looks , to offer them at some gay carriage ; but alas ! there were many bolder beggars there , gipsies who promised husbands , and other adepts in their trade , and although some ladies smiled gently as they shook their heads , and others cried to the gentlemen beside them they let the pretty face pass on , and never thought that it looked tired or hungry .
