# text = Mrs Quilp too was the partner of young Trent , and for every look that passed between them , and every word they spoke , and every card they played , the dwarf had eyes and ears ; not occupied alone with what was passing above the table , but with signals that might be exchanging beneath it , which he laid all kinds of traps to detect ; besides often treading on his wife's toes to see whether she cried out or remained silent under the infliction , in which latter case it would have been quite clear that Trent had been treading on her toes before .
