# text = She received Nell's apology for being so late with perfect good humour , and said that she should not have roused her if she had slept on until noon said the lady of the caravan asked Nell replied Mrs Jarley , with the air of a martyr Remembering the snores which had proceeded from that cleft in the caravan in which the proprietress of the wax-work passed the night , Nell rather thought she must have been dreaming of lying awake .
