# text = Mrs Jarley's back being then towards him , the military gentleman shook his forefinger as a sign that her myrmidons were not to apprise her of his presence , and stealing up close behind her , tapped her on the neck , and cried playfully cried the lady of the wax-work Pon my soul and honour ,' said Mr Slum , ' that's a good remark George received this advance with a surly indifference , observing that he was well enough for the matter of that , and hammering lustily all the time said the military gentleman turning to Mrs Jarley -- '' pon my soul and honour I hardly know what I came here for .
