# text = It made her very sad to know that this was so -- so sad to see it that sometimes when he sat idly by , smiling and nodding to her when she looked round , or when he caressed some little child and carried it to and fro , as he was fond of doing by the hour together , perplexed by its simple questions , yet patient under his own infirmity , and seeming almost conscious of it too , and humbled even before the mind of an infant -- so sad it made her to see him thus , that she would burst into tears , and , withdrawing into some secret place , fall down upon her knees and pray that he might be restored .
