# text = The other man , whom his companion had called Isaac , was of a more slender figure -- stooping , and high in the shoulders -- with a very ill-favoured face , and a most sinister and villainous squint said Isaac , looking round returned the old man said the other , interrupting him said the old man , looking anxiously at the cards retorted the other said the stout man , raising his eyes from his cards for the first time The landlord , who had apparently resolved to remain neutral until he knew which side of the question the stout man would espouse , chimed in at this place with sneered Isaac in reply , mimicking as nearly as he could , in his shrill voice , the tones of the landlord said the landlord .
