# text = Sometimes one would look up to smile to another , or to snuff the feeble candle , or to glance at the lightning as it shot through the open window and fluttering curtain , or to listen to some louder peal of thunder than the rest , with a kind of momentary impatience , as if it put him out ; but there they sat , with a calm indifference to everything but their cards , perfect philosophers in appearance , and with no greater show of passion or excitement than if they had been made of stone .
