# text = In face she bore a striking resemblance to her brother , Sampson -- so exact , indeed , was the likeness between them , that had it consorted with Miss Brass's maiden modesty and gentle womanhood to have assumed her brother's clothes in a frolic and sat down beside him , it would have been difficult for the oldest friend of the family to determine which was Sampson and which Sally , especially as the lady carried upon her upper lip certain reddish demonstrations , which , if the imagination had been assisted by her attire , might have been mistaken for a beard .
# sent_id = 1572
