# text = Is it my fault said Miss Sally , smiling drily , for she delighted in nothing so much as irritating her brother said Brass said his sister sneered Sampson Brass , reaching over to take up the bill-book , and fluttering its leaves rapidly Miss Sally deigned to make no reply , but smiled again , and went on with her work resumed Brass after a short silence returned his sister composedly Sampson Brass , who was at heart in great fear of his sister , sulkily bent over his writing again , and listened as she said Mr Brass received this observation with increased meekness , merely remarking , under his breath , that he didn't like that kind of joking , and that Miss Sally would be ' a much better fellow ' if she forbore to aggravate him .
