# text = It was a maxim with Mr Brass that the habit of paying compliments kept a man's tongue oiled without any expense ; and , as that useful member ought never to grow rusty or creak in turning on its hinges in the case of a practitioner of the law , in whom it should be always glib and easy , he lost few opportunities of improving himself by the utterance of handsome speeches and eulogistic expressions .
