# text = It was not badly named in one respect , being in truth a particularly little Bethel -- a Bethel of the smallest dimensions -- with a small number of small pews , and a small pulpit , in which a small gentleman ( by trade a Shoemaker , and by calling a Divine ) was delivering in a by no means small voice , a by no means small sermon , judging of its dimensions by the condition of his audience , which , if their gross amount were but small , comprised a still smaller number of hearers , as the majority were slumbering .
