# text = So saying , Kit marched out of the chapel , followed by his mother and little Jacob , and found himself in the open air , with an indistinct recollection of having seen the people wake up and look surprised , and of Quilp having remained , throughout the interruption , in his old attitude , without moving his eyes from the ceiling , or appearing to take the smallest notice of anything that passed said his mother , with her handkerchief to her eyes said Mrs Nubbles retorted Kit Talking on in this way , half in jest and half in earnest , and cheering up his mother , the children , and himself , by the one simple process of determining to be in a good humour , Kit led them briskly forward ; and on the road home , he related what had passed at the Notary's house , and the purpose with which he had intruded on the solemnities of Little Bethel .
