# text = Although Mr List and Mr Jowl addressed themselves to each other , it was remarkable that they both looked narrowly at the old man , who , with his eyes fixed upon the fire , sat brooding over it , yet listening eagerly -- as it seemed from a certain involuntary motion of the head , or twitching of the face from time to time -- to all they said said Jowl , lying down again with a careless air returned the person addressed said Jowl cried Isaac List rapturously said the old man , who had risen and taken two or three hurried steps away , and now returned as hurriedly cried Isaac , jumping up and slapping him on the shoulder said the old man , pointing to him eagerly with his shrivelled hand returned Isaac said Jowl with feigned reluctance said the old man urged Jowl said the old man said Jowl
