# text = But as they drew nearer the ruined walls , the moon rose in all her gentle glory , and , from their venerable age , garlanded with ivy , moss , and waving grass , the child looked back upon the sleeping town , deep in the valley's shade : and on the far-off river with its winding track of light : and on the distant hills ; and as she did so , she clasped the hand she held , less firmly , and bursting into tears , fell upon the old man's neck Her momentary weakness past , the child again summoned the resolution which had until now sustained her , and , endeavouring to keep steadily in her view the one idea that they were flying from disgrace and crime , and that her grandfather's preservation must depend solely on her firmness , unaided by one word of advice or any helping hand , urged him onward and looked back no more .
