# text = In the pale moonlight , which lent a wanness of its own to the delicate face where thoughtful care already mingled with the winning grace and loveliness of youth , the too bright eye , the spiritual head , the lips that pressed each other with such high resolve and courage of the heart , the slight figure firm in its bearing and yet so very weak , told their silent tale ; but told it only to the wind that rustled by , which , taking up its burden , carried , perhaps to some mother's pillow , faint dreams of childhood fading in its bloom , and resting in the sleep that knows no waking .
