# text = The throng of people hurried by , in two opposite streams , with no symptom of cessation or exhaustion ; intent upon their own affairs ; and undisturbed in their business speculations , by the roar of carts and waggons laden with clashing wares , the slipping of horses' feet upon the wet and greasy pavement , the rattling of the rain on windows and umbrella-tops , the jostling of the more impatient passengers , and all the noise and tumult of a crowded street in the high tide of its occupation : while the two poor strangers , stunned and bewildered by the hurry they beheld but had no part in , looked mournfully on ; feeling , amidst the crowd , a solitude which has no parallel but in the thirst of the shipwrecked mariner , who , tost to and fro upon the billows of a mighty ocean , his red eyes blinded by looking on the water which hems him in on every side , has not one drop to cool his burning tongue .
