# text = A long suburb of red brick houses -- some with patches of garden-ground , where coal-dust and factory smoke darkened the shrinking leaves , and coarse rank flowers , and where the struggling vegetation sickened and sank under the hot breath of kiln and furnace , making them by its presence seem yet more blighting and unwholesome than in the town itself -- a long , flat , straggling suburb passed , they came , by slow degrees , upon a cheerless region , where not a blade of grass was seen to grow , where not a bud put forth its promise in the spring , where nothing green could live but on the surface of the stagnant pools , which here and there lay idly sweltering by the black road-side .
