# text = The waking from a sound nap as the mail came dashing past like a highway comet , with gleaming lamps and rattling hoofs , and visions of a guard behind , standing up to keep his feet warm , and of a gentleman in a fur cap opening his eyes and looking wild and stupefied -- the stopping at the turnpike where the man was gone to bed , and knocking at the door until he answered with a smothered shout from under the bed-clothes in the little room above , where the faint light was burning , and presently came down , night-capped and shivering , to throw the gate wide open , and wish all waggons off the road except by day .
