# text = It was a very aged , ghostly place ; the church had been built many hundreds of years ago , and had once had a convent or monastery attached ; for arches in ruins , remains of oriel windows , and fragments of blackened walls , were yet standing -, while other portions of the old building , which had crumbled away and fallen down , were mingled with the churchyard earth and overgrown with grass , as if they too claimed a burying-place and sought to mix their ashes with the dust of men .
