# text = The dwarf put his hand to his great flapped ear , and counterfeited the closest attention cried Quilp , nodding his head said Quilp , conferring with himself , in imitation of his friend Mr Sampson Brass said the single gentleman rejoined Quilp said the single gentleman angrily said Quilp , with the same exasperating composure said the single gentleman , sternly regarding him cried Quilp returned his questioner , fretted into a state of the utmost irritation said Quilp , still perfectly unmoved That Quilp lied most heartily in this speech , it needed no very great penetration to discover , although for anything that he suffered to appear in his face , voice , or manner , he might have been clinging to the truth with the quiet constancy of a martyr said the unfortunate single gentleman replied Quilp , shrugging up his shoulders returned the other , throwing himself impatiently upon a sofa returned Quilp With these parting words , and with a grin upon his features altogether indescribable , but which seemed to be compounded of every monstrous grimace of which men or monkeys are capable , the dwarf slowly retreated and closed the door behind him he said when he had regained his own room , and sat himself down in a chair with his arms akimbo Chuckling as though in very great glee , and recompensing himself for the restraint he had lately put upon his countenance by twisting it into all imaginable varieties of ugliness , Mr Quilp , rocking himself to and fro in his chair and nursing his left leg at the same time , fell into certain meditations , of which it may be necessary to relate the substance .
