# text = Kit stood his ground as if in expectation of an immediate assault , but finding that nothing came of these gestures , snapped his fingers and walked away ; his mother dragging him off as fast as she could , and , even in the midst of his news of little Jacob and the baby , looking anxiously over her shoulder to see if Quilp were following Kit's mother might have spared herself the trouble of looking back so often , for nothing was further from Mr Quilp's thoughts than any intention of pursuing her and her son , or renewing the quarrel with which they had parted .
