# text = The other gentleman assented , observing that he was expected at the Hospital , and that several pensioners would be ready to receive him whenever he arrived said Mr Brass assented Mrs Jiniwin hastily said Sampson Brass , taking up his pen said Mrs Jiniwin said Brass , in an insinuating tone observed Mrs Quilp with a sob said Brass , writing as he spoke Very crooked ,' suggested Mrs Jiniwin said Brass piously said the old lady muttered Quilp said the lawyer , laying down his pen and emptying his glass said Mr Brass smiling fondly at the wall said Mrs Jiniwin impatiently cried Mr Brass said Mrs Jiniwin cried Quilp , thrusting in his head , and striking the feature with his fist shouted Brass , from the mere force of habit Quilp paid no regard whatever to these compliments , nor to the dubious and frightened look into which the lawyer gradually subsided , nor to the shrieks of his wife and mother-in-law , nor to the latter's running from the room , nor to the former's fainting away .
