# text = Therefore , he stood as far off as he could , while the dwarf was thus engaged ; whimpering out but feeble applause ; and when Quilp left off and sat down again from pure exhaustion , approached with more obsequiousness than ever cried Brass said Sampson , looking round as if in appeal to the bruised animal said the dwarf cried Brass said Quilp , beckoning him to draw near said Quilp returned Brass , looking timidly at the dwarf's cunning eyes , which were turned towards the fire and reflected its red light inquired Quilp , without looking up returned Brass , venturing to be more familiar said Quilp , looking up with a perfectly vacant countenance cried Brass , nodding his head retorted Quilp returned Brass said the dwarf , looking about him as if for his poker rejoined Brass , checking himself with great alacrity said Quilp , heating some rum in a little saucepan , and watching it to prevent its boiling over returned Brass said the dwarf , stopping his hand in the act of carrying the saucepan to his mouth said Brass Deigning no other than a practical answer to this remonstrance , Mr Quilp raised the hot saucepan to his lips , and deliberately drank off all the spirit it contained , which might have been in quantity about half a pint , and had been but a moment before , when he took it off the fire , bubbling and hissing fiercely .
